    "updated_at": "2021-04-23T01:49:50Z",
    "body": "> Is there a way to fix or optimize this?\r\n\r\nWriting blindly (can't test it on a real machine) but this should work:\r\n```toml\r\n[custom.test_ps]\r\ncommand = \"write-host test\"\r\nwhen = \"0\"\r\nshell = [\"cmd.exe\", \"/C\"]\r\nformat = \"[$output]($style) \"\r\nstyle = \"bright-yellow\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n> How can I find out which shell is spawned?\r\n\r\nHuh, ask me an easier question please :sweat_smile: I'm afraid there is no easy way, that info doesn't get traced so tweaking `STARSHIP_LOG` won't help you there. Maybe switching command with `echo %0` but that is just a very wild guess.",
